Each skeleton point carries x, y and a width multiplier for the LEFT and for the RIGHT side of the stroke, so a stroke can take any silhouette; --subdivide inserts more points between the fitted ones and fits again.
A Python port of strokePolygon() in motion/runtime/zs-templates-brushfont-1.js (checked against node by --check). Prints the fitted glyph lines in JS source form and, with --apply, patches them into the font file.
Run with /Users/zenray/.venvs/zenray-motion/bin/python -I.
Usage: ZhongKuiFontFit.py [--letters ZHONGKUI] [--passes 4] [--subdivide 2] [--tol 2.5] [--apply] [--check] [--score FILE.json] [--lock N:1,K:2]"""
